# Base:  kexts/NVRMAGDC after 0004 (NvGfx xe 0.0.44)
# Files: kexts/NVRMAGDC/nvrm-agdc.cpp, kexts/NVRMAGDC/xe/Info.plist,
#        kexts/NVRMAGDC/xe/firmware-timing.h, kexts/NVRMAGDC/xe/panel-timing.h (removed)
# Apply: patch -p1 -E < patches/0013-agdc-m3d-in-kernel-arm.patch   (-E removes the two emptied headers)
#
# - The adapter is a direct IOFramebuffer subclass that serviceMatching("IONDRVFramebuffer") never sees, so both
#   classes are enumerated; the legacy one stays first while IntelFB and the adapter are both loaded.
# - The two userspace steps (sysctl debug.xegfx_agdc=1 and debug.xegfx_agdc_k5=1) get an in-kernel replacement:
#   the boot-armed accelerator's XeGfxAccelAgdcRequest is read from the PCI node (and again on the 0x980 path),
#   an auto poll arms AGDC once a framebuffer exists, and the K5 half applies even after userspace armed it.
# - The fixed firmware/panel timing headers from 0004 are gone; the boot framebuffer's timing is the panel's
#   native mode as published for the same panel.  Read-only observables are published for the boot guard.
#
